19:T73d,## 1. Clarify requirements (always do this first)

- A **bank** of several elevators serving a building.
- **Hall buttons** (up / down) on each floor; **cabin buttons** inside each car for destinations.
- Serve every request **efficiently**, minimise waiting and travel.
- Each car moves **up**, **down**, or sits **idle**.

State the assumptions out loud, number of cars, number of floors, optimise-for-wait vs optimise-for-throughput.

## 2. Find the nouns → the classes

`ElevatorSystem` (the dispatcher / entry point), `Elevator` (its current floor, direction and a queue of pending stops), `Request` (a floor + a direction), and a `DispatchStrategy`. Hall and cabin presses are just `Button`s feeding requests in.

The system **owns** its elevators (composition) and **holds** a dispatch strategy it can swap.

## 3. Each elevator is a state machine

A single car is a tiny **state machine**: `Idle → MovingUp → MovingDown → Idle`. While `MovingUp` it serves every up-stop in order (SCAN) before it ever considers reversing. Modelling direction as explicit states keeps the per-car logic clean.

## 4. The scheduler is a Strategy

The genuinely interesting decision, **which car answers a hall call**, lives behind a `DispatchStrategy` interface. Plug in **nearest-car**, or **LOOK / SCAN** (elevator-algorithm) scheduling, without touching the system. This is the Strategy pattern: policy swappable independent of mechanism.

```
interface DispatchStrategy {
    Elevator pick(Request r, List<Elevator> cars);
}
```

## 5. Mention the hard part

**Scheduling is the open-ended, genuinely hard part** — there is no single right answer. Nearest-car is greedy and starves; SCAN/LOOK is fairer but more complex. Call this out: separating the *policy* (which car) from the *mechanism* (how a car moves) is exactly what lets you tune it later.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-case-studies","activeLesson":"elevator-system"}],["$","$L18","elevator-system",{"lesson":{"id":"elevator-system","patternId":"lld-case-studies","title":"Design an Elevator System","kind":"case-study","difficulty":"Advanced","statement":"Multiple elevators, hall and cabin requests, and a scheduler that decides which car goes where, modelled with a direction State machine and a pluggable dispatch Strategy.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Uber"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"Model the system","code":["class ElevatorSystem {","    List<Elevator> elevators;","    DispatchStrategy dispatch;","    void request(int floor, Dir dir) {","        Elevator e = dispatch.pick(new Request(floor, dir));","        e.addStop(floor);","    }","}"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":4,"narration":"ElevatorSystem is the entry point. It receives hall requests and delegates the genuinely hard \"which car?\" decision rather than deciding inline.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"sys","name":"ElevatorSystem","methods":["+ request(floor, dir)"],"x":0,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"sched","name":"Dispatcher","stereotype":"interface","methods":["+ pick(req): Elevator"],"x":1.3,"y":0.2,"tint":"accent2"},{"id":"req","name":"Request","fields":["- floor","- dir"],"x":2.5,"y":0.2},{"id":"elev","name":"Elevator","fields":["- floor","- dir","- stops"],"methods":["+ addStop(f)"],"x":0.4,"y":1.55},{"id":"btn","name":"Button","fields":["- floor"],"x":1.9,"y":1.55}],"relations":[{"id":"r1","from":"sys","to":"elev","kind":"compose","label":"elevators *"},{"id":"r2","from":"sys","to":"sched","kind":"aggregate","label":"dispatch"},{"id":"r3","from":"sys","to":"req","kind":"depend"},{"id":"r4","from":"elev","to":"btn","kind":"aggregate"}],"shownClassIds":["sys"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["sys"]},"vars":[["requirement","route requests to cars"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"The Dispatcher is a Strategy, nearest-car / SCAN / LOOK, swappable without touching the system. An Elevator tracks its floor, direction and pending stops.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["sys","sched","elev"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2"],"activeIds":["sched","elev"]},"vars":[["Strategy","Dispatcher"],["Elevator","floor · dir · stops"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Requests come from hall + cabin Buttons; the system keeps the POLICY (dispatch) separate from the MECHANISM (the elevators that actually move). That seam is the whole design.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["sys","sched","req","elev","btn"],"shownRelIds":["r1","r2","r3","r4"],"activeIds":["req","btn"]},"vars":[["policy","Dispatcher"],["mechanism","Elevator"]]}]},{"label":"An elevator's direction","code":["enum Dir { IDLE, UP, DOWN }","","class Elevator {","    int floor; Dir dir = IDLE;","    TreeSet<Integer> stops;   // served in SCAN order","}"],"steps":[{"view":"state","narration":"At rest the car sits Idle on some floor, no pending stops, no direction.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":1.1,"y":0,"kind":"start"},{"id":"up","label":"MovingUp","x":0,"y":1},{"id":"down","label":"MovingDown","x":2.2,"y":1}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"up","label":"up request"},{"id":"e2","from":"up","to":"idle","label":"no more up stops"},{"id":"e3","from":"idle","to":"down","label":"down request"},{"id":"e4","from":"down","to":"idle","label":"no more down stops"}],"activeId":"idle","firedEdgeId":"$undefined","label":"one car's direction"},"vars":[["start","Idle"]]},{"view":"state","codeLine":4,"narration":"A request above arrives → the car goes MovingUp (fire e1), serving every up-stop in order on the way (SCAN, it never reverses mid-sweep).","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":1.1,"y":0,"kind":"start"},{"id":"up","label":"MovingUp","x":0,"y":1},{"id":"down","label":"MovingDown","x":2.2,"y":1}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"up","label":"up request"},{"id":"e2","from":"up","to":"idle","label":"no more up stops"},{"id":"e3","from":"idle","to":"down","label":"down request"},{"id":"e4","from":"down","to":"idle","label":"no more down stops"}],"activeId":"up","firedEdgeId":"e1","label":"one car's direction"},"vars":[["Idle + up req","→ MovingUp"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Once the up-queue empties it returns to Idle (fire e2), or, if down-requests are waiting, it switches to MovingDown instead and sweeps the other way.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":1.1,"y":0,"kind":"start"},{"id":"up","label":"MovingUp","x":0,"y":1},{"id":"down","label":"MovingDown","x":2.2,"y":1}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"up","label":"up request"},{"id":"e2","from":"up","to":"idle","label":"no more up stops"},{"id":"e3","from":"idle","to":"down","label":"down request"},{"id":"e4","from":"down","to":"idle","label":"no more down stops"}],"activeId":"idle","firedEdgeId":"e2","label":"one car's direction"},"vars":[["up queue empty","→ Idle / MovingDown"]]},{"view":"state","narration":"Each elevator is its OWN state machine driving its direction; the Dispatcher (the Strategy) decides WHICH elevator takes a new hall call. Policy and mechanism, cleanly split.","state":{"nodes":[{"id":"idle","label":"Idle","x":1.1,"y":0,"kind":"start"},{"id":"up","label":"MovingUp","x":0,"y":1},{"id":"down","label":"MovingDown","x":2.2,"y":1}],"edges":[{"id":"e1","from":"idle","to":"up","label":"up request"},{"id":"e2","from":"up","to":"idle","label":"no more up stops"},{"id":"e3","from":"idle","to":"down","label":"down request"},{"id":"e4","from":"down","to":"idle","label":"no more down stops"}],"activeId":"idle","firedEdgeId":"$undefined","label":"one car's direction"},"vars":[["policy vs mechanism",""],["Strategy + State","✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
